# Masterpiece Editorial Standard

Today's Masterpiece is a **signature editorial feature**. Every article reads
like a beautifully edited **museum magazine** — Smithsonian, Apollo, or an
exhibition catalog — **not** a generic encyclopedia entry or AI summary.

**Constitution:** `kindred-editorial-constitution.mdc` — never invent history;
every factual claim from verified museum or scholarly sources.

## General principles

- Never repeat information across sections
- Each section teaches something **new**
- Lead with **facts before interpretation**
- Explain **why the artwork matters**
- Tone: educational, timeless, accessible
- Never invent history or speculate
- Target **1,200–2,000 words** when verified material supports it
- If confidence is low, **omit** — do not pad

## Section architecture (publish order)

| # | Section | Job |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | **Overview** (`Introduction`) | 2–3 factual paragraphs: what, who, when, movement, medium, where displayed, why important. **Begin with knowledge** — never "Step closer…" or emotional invitations |
| 2 | **About the Artist** | Birthplace, period, influences, innovations, famous works, legacy — no repeats from Overview |
| 3 | **Historical Context** | Political, cultural, religious, scientific, societal context — **why this artwork existed** |
| 4 | **The Story Behind the Artwork** | Commission, purpose, subjects, action, symbolism, reception, controversies |
| 5 | **Looking Closer** | Composition, perspective, light, color, brushwork, symbolism, hidden details — each paragraph teaches observation |
| 6 | **Legacy** | Influence on artists, art history, museum significance, culture, scholarship |
| 7 | **Did You Know?** | **3–5** verified surprising facts — no filler (single blob today → expand at ingest) |
| 8 | **Where to See It Today** | Museum, city, country, official website — encourage seeing the original |
| 9 | **Editorial Reflection** | **Only** Kindred voice: one thoughtful paragraph on curiosity, learning, observation. No fact repeats, no summary |
| 10 | **Artwork Credits** | Title, artist, year, medium, museum, image source, license, official link |

## Quality rules

- Every section introduces **new** information
- Never restate facts already covered
- Reader should finish feeling they **genuinely learned** something new

## Implementation map

| Concern | Location |
| --- | --- |
| Ingest validation | `heroArtwork/detailEditorial.ts` — `isMasterpieceDetailComplete()` |
| Detail assembly | `heroArtwork/detailTemplate.ts`, `presentation.ts` |
